# CODEOWNERS: reviewers GitHub requests automatically for security-sensitive paths.
# With branch protection's "Require review from Code Owners", one listed owner
# (other than the PR author) must approve changes to these paths.
# Team convention on top of that: security-sensitive PRs need TWO approvals (see CONTRIBUTING.md).
#
# Owners are the four team members (usernames verified from commits and organization invitations):
#   arhamnasirkhan, ammarusmani729, AnushaAbbasy, WaniyaSiddiqui.
# Code owners must be members of the blood-connect-team organization with write access;
# owners who have not joined yet are ignored by GitHub until they do.
# After pushing, check Settings → Code / the CODEOWNERS file view for syntax errors.
#
# Paths not listed here have no code owner: any team member may review them.
# When several patterns match, the LAST matching line wins.

